# Svelte-LiveView Integration Guidelines

## Project Structure

### File Organization
- Keep Svelte components in `assets/svelte/` directory
- Organize components by feature/domain
- Use consistent naming conventions:
  - Component files: `PascalCase.svelte`
  - Component directories: `kebab-case/`
  - Utility files: `camelCase.js`

### Component Structure
```svelte
<script>
  // Props should be reactive and documented
  export let number = 1
  export let live // LiveView socket connection

  // Local state management
  let localState = 0

  // Event handlers
  function handleEvent() {
    // Push events to LiveView
    live.pushEvent("event_name", { data: value }, () => {
      // Optional callback
    })
  }
</script>

<!-- Template -->
<div class="component-container">
  <!-- Component content -->
</div>

<!-- Scoped styles -->
<style>
  .component-container {
    /* Component-specific styles */
  }
</style>
```

## State Management

### LiveView Integration
- Use `live.pushEvent()` for server communication
- Keep client-side state minimal
- Leverage LiveView's real-time capabilities
- Use proper event naming conventions:
  - `handle_` prefix for event handlers
  - `update_` prefix for state updates
  - `sync_` prefix for data synchronization

### Props Management
```elixir
# LiveView module
def render(assigns) do
  ~H"""
  <.svelte 
    name="ComponentName" 
    props={%{
      data: @data,
      options: @options
    }} 
    socket={@socket} 
  />
  """
end
```

## Performance Optimization

### Component Loading
- Use `:loading` slot for better UX
- Implement proper loading states
- Use SSR when possible
- Optimize component initialization

```svelte
<.svelte name="Component" ssr={false}>
  <:loading>
    <div class="loading-state">
      <!-- Loading content -->
    </div>
  </:loading>
</.svelte>
```

### Event Handling
- Implement proper event throttling
- Use debouncing for search inputs
- Optimize event payload size
- Handle errors gracefully

